#
# Declining-balance depreciation, in Sutra (neap_rules.h NR4): one
# period's charge on an asset whose book value at the period's start is
# book, at rate hundredths of a percent, never below salvage: the last
# period (last 1) takes what is left above salvage, any other book * rate
# / 10000 truncated as COMPUTE does (the floor: nothing is negative), at
# most what is left. book and salvage fit 9(12); room (book - salvage),
# top (10000 - rate) and once (1 - last) are unsigned, so a salvage past
# the book, a rate past 100 percent or a last flag past 1 is a size error,
# refused. declining.tb takes a book to 15 digits: past 12 the two
# disagree, held.
record neap-declining
  book: 9(12)
  salvage: 9(12)
  rate: 9(5)
  last: 9(1)
  room: 9(12)
  top: 9(5)
  once: 9(1)
  charge: 9(12)
procedure
  compute room = book - salvage
  compute top = 10000 - rate
  compute once = 1 - last
  if last = 1
    answer room
  end-if
  compute charge = book * rate / 10000
  if charge > room
    answer room
  end-if
  answer charge
